  "known_limitations": {
    "three_defects_fixed_on_landing": "The branch did not pass its own suite as written, and its PR disclosed a failure and errors rather than hiding them. All three are fixed here. First, banking_sandbox.py pinned CHART_SHA256 to a digest that matches nothing: the campaign finance ledger's accounts.bean is byte-identical at the commit the file pins as LEDGER_BASE_COMMIT, on the ledger branch, and on main, and hashes to c4b4578dd008be99b094845fc3e9db718326ade4f0c6ed86b9071cc13ae05940, while the pin read d0a1123. Neither the LF nor the CRLF form of the file produces the pinned value, so the pin was simply wrong rather than stale through drift. It is re-pinned to the file that exists, and the test's remaining assertions on account names and currencies pass unchanged, which is what actually proves the chart contract holds. Second and third, two subprocess acceptance tests launched the CLI as economy_impl.whole_economy_cli and put the project directory on PYTHONPATH, both correct for the flat scratch layout the code was written in and wrong for this repository's src layout. The module name is now derived from whichever package the file imported, and the import root from that package's own location, so both layouts work and the out-of-process tests can no longer pass in-process while failing in a subprocess.",
    "accounting_is_not_canonical": "The engine advances no canonical campaign time, posts to no canonical ledger, and writes nothing to Notion. Executable quantities without accepted campaign authority are marked scenario_assumption and canonical:false. Nothing here is user-visible or campaign-accepted, and landing it does not grant that acceptance.",
    "depth_gaps_the_author_declared": "Carried forward from the branch and not closed here: acreage is fiscal and does not constrain agricultural capacity or yield; arrears are recorded but do not age, service, relieve or enforce; migration moves population and labor but not proportional household wealth; wage pull is class-level rather than occupation-specific; seized collateral is held and impaired rather than liquidated; and opening bank balancing assets are explicit non-canonical assumptions.",
    "windows_launcher_not_exercised": "The project ships .cmd launchers for Windows and the branch records launcher runs on the author's Windows machine committing Months 1 to 3. That evidence is the author's and was not reproduced here; this landing exercised the Python suite on Linux only.",
    "wheel_build_not_reproduced": "VALIDATION.md records a reproducible wheel build and its SHA-256. The wheel was not rebuilt on landing. The one claim inside it that could be checked from the repository was checked: the third-party notice hash matches exactly.",
    "project_tests_are_not_in_repository_ci": "The 462 tests live under this project and are not discovered by the repository CI step, which reads only the root tests directory. They were run directly for this landing. Wiring them into CI is a separate decision and is not made here."
  },
  "notion_write": "NONE. No Notion read or write was performed by this landing."
